<title>POLAND: Polish PBG bank buys bankrupt cooperative bank.</title>
<headline>Polish PBG bank buys bankrupt cooperative bank.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned  Powszechny Bank Gospodarczy SA on Tuesday bought a bankrupt cooperative, Spoldzileczy Bank Ludowy w Lodzi, PAP news agency said.</p>
<p>It said PBG paid more than one million zlotys for the bank, which recently reported losses of 14 million zlotys.</p>
<p>PBG will meet all liabilities and, as part of the deal, it will receive an undisclosed amount of treasury bills from the central bank, it said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
